course: dictionary
lesson: 2644
title: Detective words and clues
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A detective is someone whose job is to find out who did a crime and how. Detectives look closely at clues, the small facts that point to the answer.
explain: You can be a detective outside stories too. «In an olympiad puzzle about soft words you are a detective: first turn every soft phrase into plain words.» Looking for clues to solve a puzzle is detective work.
explain: «Detective» can also be an adjective, describing things about solving crimes. A «detective story» is a mystery book, and «detective work» is the careful searching for clues. «A detective does not need a magnifying glass, only careful eyes.»
fact: A detective is a police officer or private worker who finds out who did a crime and how.
fact: Anyone who looks closely at clues to solve a puzzle or mystery can be a detective.
fact: As an adjective, «detective story» and «detective work» are about solving crimes.
fact: Useful phrases are «private detective», «play detective» and «do some detective work».
fact: «Detective» is a noun, and its plural is «detectives».
exercise: «A detective does not need a magnifying glass, only careful eyes.» What does a detective need most? | *Careful eyes | A loud voice | A police car | A large magnifying glass
exercise: In maths, «be a maths detective» means what? | Count how many pencils you have | *Look for clues in a problem to find the answer | Ask your teacher for help straight away | Draw a picture of a crime scene
exercise: What does «detective» mean in «detective story»? | A story about cooking | A story about the sea | *A story about solving crimes | A story about gardening
test: «Koalas have fingerprints so like ours that they could confuse a detective.» What could confuse a detective? | A sunny day at the beach | A bowl of eucalyptus leaves | A loud noise in the bush | *Koala fingerprints, which are so like ours
test: What is the job of a detective? | To cook food in a busy kitchen | To paint pictures for a museum | To fly planes across the sea | *To find out who did a crime and how
exam: «In an olympiad puzzle about soft words you are a detective: first turn every soft phrase into plain words.» What should you do first? | Guess the answer without reading | Draw a picture of the puzzle | Skip the puzzle completely | *Turn every soft phrase into plain words
